{"kind":"request","text":"claude: durable cleanup for the two decision-records lanes that are finished in substance but still open on the board. No code, no branch, no gates — this is records only, and it clears four rows.\n\nWHY THESE TWO ROWS ARE STILL OPEN, WHICH IS MY DOING. 160c9acb and 54c40bf9 have both sat reported and unratifiable for most of today, and I have asserted twice about why without ever asking anyone to close them. An assert explains a row; it does not clear one.\n\n160c9acb IS FINISHED AND HAS BEEN SINCE 02:10. The receipt-checkpoint rule is in main. It did not merge as the head you reported, 4981c6d0 — it merged as candidate 10c6d623 under 2031cdfb, after the authorized recut on child cc20c44a. I know that better than most because I filed a request this morning telling you to redo that work, having read a stale verdict and not checked whether its blocker still existed. This request is the opposite of that one: it asks only for the paperwork the merge left behind.\n\nThat paperwork matters here more than usual. The three merged successors at internal/workroom, docs/reference/gs/merge.md and docs/concepts/staleness.md are live and fresh right now — I checked before writing this, and they are the bases this request rests on. The five artifacts at 4981c6d0 sit alongside them at the same paths, abandoned but live, which is the two-candidates-at-one-path shape that has cost this board several lanes today. Retiring them is not tidiness; it is removing a trap.\n\n54c40bf9 IS DEAD RATHER THAN DELIVERED, and I want that distinction kept in the record. Its head 3fd75543 got a ratified changes-requested, my successor request d14e96fb said in its own conditions not to merge or ratify it, and the work moved on twice since. So step (4) asks you explicitly NOT to report against it. I will retire it myself once its three artifacts are gone — in that order, because retiring the request first would stale the artifacts where they stand instead of clearing them.\n\nI have listed eight artifacts from a path query. If the query missed one, or you find one already retired, say so and act on what is actually there rather than on my list. I would rather this took one extra record than left a straggler at a path someone opens a lane on next week.","body":{"conditions":"Durable records only — no branch, no code, no gates. (1) Bare-supersede, with no successors, the five abandoned artifacts at head 4981c6d0: 0c0c5bce at internal/workroom, 1bc530db at internal/app, 2c556762 at docs/reference/architecture.md, 17124e24 at docs/reference/gs/merge.md, 398dc206 at docs/concepts/staleness.md. That head never merged; the behaviour shipped instead as candidate 10c6d623 under merge 2031cdfb, whose successors at three of those paths are live and fresh today. (2) Bare-supersede, with no successors, the three abandoned artifacts at head 3fd75543: 30a672a6 at docs/reference/architecture.md, 862e8bb5 at ui, 12e36238 at internal/service. That head is the one my request d14e96fb explicitly told you not to merge or ratify. (3) File one explicit report against my request 160c9acb, closing it on merged main. Name merge 2031cdfb and candidate 10c6d623, and state plainly that reported head 4981c6d0 is not in main and never will be, so the closure is by the substance having shipped under a different candidate rather than by that head being accepted. Carry no body.verdict: this is a closure report, not a review. I will ratify it. (4) Do NOT file a report against 54c40bf9. Its lane is dead rather than delivered and I will retire the request myself once step (2) is done; a report there would claim a satisfaction nobody should record. (5) If any artifact I have named is already retired, or you find a further live artifact at either head that I have missed, say so on this row and retire it too rather than stopping at my list — I built it from a path query and it may not be complete.","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}